#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""devin-sync — keep local Devin Desktop / Devin CLI sessions in sync between Linux PCs
through any folder-sync service (Nextcloud, Syncthing, Dropbox, ...).

Devin only syncs *cloud* sessions. Local ones live in SQLite files that must not be
symlinked into a synced folder (WAL + partial uploads = silent corruption). This wrapper
instead takes a consistent snapshot when Devin closes and merges it in when Devin opens.

What is synced (local path -> <sync_dir>/data/...):
  ~/.local/share/devin/cli/sessions.db       sessions.db   session-level merge, newest wins
  state.vscdb rows 'windsurf.acp.*'          index.json    sidebar index / message-store map
  ~/.config/Devin/User/acp-messages/*.db     acp-messages/ per-file, newest mtime wins
  ~/.codeium/windsurf/{cascade,memories}     cascade/ memories/   (legacy Windsurf Cascade chats)
  ~/.windsurf/plans                          plans/
  ~/.config/Devin/User/{settings,keybindings}.json, snippets/   user/
Never synced: the rest of state.vscdb (keyring-encrypted login), Electron profile, caches.

Usage:
  devin-sync install --sync-dir DIR   once per PC: config, ~/.local/bin shim, menu launcher
  devin-sync desktop [args]           pull -> run Devin Desktop -> push when every Devin process exits
  devin-sync cli [args]               same, for the Devin CLI
  devin-sync sync                     pull + push now (Devin must be closed)
  devin-sync status                   lock / snapshot / local state
  devin-sync uninstall                remove shim and launcher override (synced data is kept)
  --force                             ignore a lock held by another PC

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
"""
